## 2) Method Catalog

## 2.1 Supabase (RLS-first)
Key extraction:
- APK BuildConfig.java
- JS bundles / Next.js `_next/static` / source maps
- console logs / service-worker scope

Schema discovery:
- OpenAPI: `GET /rest/v1/` + anon key
- RPC probe: `POST /rest/v1/rpc/<function>` (vary JSON shapes)

Data reachability:
- Table probe: `GET /rest/v1/<table>?select=<col>&limit=1`
- Write proof (safe): `POST/PATCH/DELETE` to sandbox table only

Privilege patterns:
- `SECURITY DEFINER` function + caller-controlled tenant ID
- `auth.uid()` null-bypass patterns in PL/pgSQL

Storage:
- Enumerate buckets: `GET /storage/v1/bucket`
- List files: `GET /storage/v1/object/list/<bucket>`
- Public read test: `HEAD /storage/v1/object/<bucket>/<path>`

Realtime:
- Socket handshake + channel subscribe (PASSIVE read only)

## 2.2 Firebase
Recon:
- `google-services.json` / `GoogleService-Info.plist`
- JS `firebaseConfig`

Checks:
- Realtime DB: `GET https://<project>.firebaseio.com/.json`
- Firestore REST: `GET .../databases/(default)/documents`
- Storage listing: `GET https://storage.googleapis.com/<bucket>/`

Auth probes:
- `identitytoolkit` signUp / signInWithPassword (proof-only, no mass-attack)
- Token decode (non-destructive)

## 2.3 WordPress + XML-RPC
Enumeration:
- `/robots.txt`, `/readme.html`, `/wp-json/wp/v2/users`
- `/?author=1` redirect chain

XMLRPC (proof-only):
- `GET /xmlrpc.php` (405 = present)
- `POST` method: `wp.getUsersBlogs` (fault证实 method exposed)
- `system.multicall` amplification proof (3-method sample)

## 2.4 Auth Bypass / Credential Testing
Methods:
- SQLi login bypass patterns
- Account enumeration via message deltas
- Password reset token predictability/reuse/host-header injection
- Brute-force resistance mapping + lockout bypass patterns
- 2FA skip paths and code reuse checks
- OAuth/SSO takeover patterns

## 2.5 Android Binary + MITM
Workflow:
- Original APK install + login capture
- Patched APK with CA injection -> capture replay kit
- Replay with curl + headers to isolate server-side weaknesses

## 3) Exploit Chain Templates

### A) Supabase Read -> Full Schema -> Targeted Dump
1. Extract anon key
2. OpenAPI schema enumeration
3. Table reachability probe
4. Identify RLS gaps or function misuse
5. Export only needed proof rows
6. Remediation SQL + commit path

### B) Firebase Public DB -> Auth Path -> Token Abuse
1. Check `.json` root
2. Enumerate paths
3. Auth probe for weaker sign-in surfaces
4. Decode tokens (non-destructive)
5. Map rule breakage to data sensitivity

### C) WordPress Subdomain -> XMLRPC -> Admin Path
1. Subdomain inventory
2. Version fingerprint
3. XMLRPC existence proof
4. Admin username enumeration
5. Lockout/rate-limit assessment
6. Hardening plan (disable xmlrpc, WAF, 2FA)

### D) Android App -> API Leak -> Server Chain
1. Extract keys/endpoints from APK
2. Replay endpoints from captured headers
3. Compare server responses by role
4. Prove IDOR / missing authZ
5. Package proof-only repro script

